 ],
 "literal": "Like streaming sapphires, the dark-vined hariali grass, / tender branches shedding their buds, along with female deer, / the male deer leaps in the forest we leave behind. / Having performed our work excellently, we return to that mountain. / 'Is it possible for you to bear this, oh one with flower-like earrings?' / Even before saying this, not stopping, / tears obstructing her sight, weeping without ceasing, / they obstructed the chariot, the young woman's eyes indeed!",
 "translation": "The male deer leaps along with his mate in the forest we leave behind, where the dark-vined hariali grass looks like streaming sapphires and tender branches shed their buds. We are returning to that mountain limit after successfully completing our task. Even before I could ask, 'Oh one with flower-like earrings, is it possible for you to bear this separation?', her eyes, weeping without ceasing and filled with obstructing tears, stood in the way of my chariot!",
 "modern": "நீலமணிகள் ஒழுகுவது போன்ற கரிய கொடிகளையுடைய அறுகம்புல்லையும், அரும்புகள் அவிழ்ந்த மெல்லிய கொம்புகளையும் பிணையோடு கூடி உண்டு ஆண்மான் துள்ளி விளையாடும் காட்டைப் பின்னே தள்ளி, நம் கடமையைச் செவ்வனே முடித்துவிட்டு அந்த மலை எல்லையை நோக்கி வருகின்றோம். 'பூங்குழையணிந்தவளே! என் பிரிவைத் தாங்கிக் கொள்ள உன்னால் இயலுமா?' என்று நான் கேட்பதற்கு முன்னரே, அவளது கண்கள் நில்லாமல் அழுது, பெருகிய கண்ணீரால் வழி மறைத்து, எனது தேரையே தடுத்து நிறுத்திவிட்டன.",
 "explanation": "The hero (தலைவன்) is returning to his beloved after successfully completing his mission in the desert/wasteland (பாலை). He remembers how, as he was about to leave, he wanted to ask her if she could bear the separation. But even before he could speak, her eyes filled with unstoppable tears, which seemed to physically block his chariot from leaving. The imagery of the fertile forest they are passing through, where the male deer leaps happily with his mate amidst lush grass and budding branches, contrasts with the painful memory of his departure. This beautiful pālai poem highlights the intense grief of separation and the deep empathy of the hero who is eager to return to his beloved.",
